<title>DENMARK: BG Bank 1996 pre-tax profit rises.</title>
<headline>BG Bank 1996 pre-tax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Result before tax and ex.items	 1,938	  vs 1,885</p>
<p> Group net result			   1,405	  vs 1,689</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions	   468	  vs   739</p>
<p> Securities and forex results	     414	  vs   884</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (percent)		 12	  vs     5</p>
<p> Net interest and fees income	   6,147   vs  5,947</p>
<p> Result of financial items		6,764   vs  7,049</p>
<p>Own capital at end-1996, 8.166 billion crowns vs 6.104 billion at end-1995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's third biggest bank is BG Bank A/S. It said in a statement that it expected slightly lower core earnings in 1997 than 1996's 1.66 billion crowns. The 1996 pre-tax result was close to analysts' average expectations of 1.972 billion crowns. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom, +45-33-969650</p>
</text>
